is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the L2/L3 bridge configuration on sshswitch, which provides the default gateways 10.5.0.254 (VLAN 5) and 10.6.0.254 (VLAN 6). Mechanism: After a reload, sshswitch is bridging the physical trunk to the access switch (eth0) together with the bond to the core (bond0) in br_v1 (mgmt), while simultaneously bridging VLAN subinterfaces eth0.5/eth0.6 with bond0.5/bond0.6 in br_v5/br_v6. With STP disabled, this creates parallel L2 paths for the same tagged frames (via br_v1 and via br_v5/br_v6), leading to L2 loops/MAC flapping and intermittent ARP failure, which presents to users as “can’t reach gateway” on both 10.5.0.x and 10.6.0.x at the same time. Localization: On sshswitch: brctl/bridge show prove
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=17
